{{Quote|Tell me how you know, Jixtus of the Grysks, ''[&hellip;]'' If the Chiss mounted a raid, there would of course be prisoners. If there was a battle, even the most fearsome often leaves survivors. Tell me now, or I shall ask him.|[[Generalirius]] [[Nakirre]], to "[[Jixtus]]"|<ref name="Lesser Evil">''[[Thrawn Ascendancy: Lesser Evil]]''</ref>}}
[[File:ZinskaFull-CGSWG.png|thumb|right|250px|[[Zinska]], a prisoner of Narkina 5]]
A '''prisoner''' was an individual who was captured and held in [[Prison|confinement]] by another party. It was considered a war crime to [[torture]] a prisoner, but several major powers, like the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="Shadow Warrior">{{TCW|Shadow Warrior}}</ref> [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> and [[First Order]] did so in secret.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|These are prisoners."''<br />''"Yes. Where are you taking them?"''<br />''"I am taking them... to imprison them. In prison.|K-2SO impersonating a real [[KX-series security droid|Imperial security droid]] while talking to a [[stormtrooper]]|<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], both the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="TJWKTM">{{TCW|The Jedi Who Knew Too Much}}</ref> and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] took prisoners.<ref name="TC">{{TCW|The Citadel (episode)}}</ref> Early in the Clone Wars, the Confederacy had [[clone trooper]]s taken to Regent [[Queb's compound]].<ref name="Battle Tales 3">[[Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales 3|''Star Wars Adventures: The Clone Wars – Battle Tales'' 3]]</ref> They also had [[Jedi]] taken to the [[Citadel]].<ref name="TC" /> The Republic kept their prisoners at the [[Imperial Inspectorate HQ|Naval Intelligence headquarters]] on Coruscant.<ref name="TJWKTM" />

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] was held prisoner by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] before she was [[Rescue of Princess Leia|rescued]] by [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Han Solo]], and [[Chewbacca]]<ref name="Episode IV" /> assigned the designation of "Prisoner 2187."<ref name="anhillustrated">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref>

The [[Galactic Empire]] used the prisoners of [[Narkina 5]] for manufacturing and labor<ref>''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' - [[Narkina 5 (episode)|Narkina 5]]</ref> until an [[Narkina 5 prison escape|escape]] took place in [[5 BBY]].<ref>''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' - [[One Way Out]]</ref> The Empire also used the prisoners of the mobile prison [[Accresker Jail]] as an [[Accresker Penal Legion|expendable fighting force]].<ref name="Aphra20">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 20|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 20]]</ref>

